# Design System Implementation Rules

## Source of Truth

- `src/theme/tokens.ts` is the source of truth for all design values in components.
- Generated from Figma via Style Dictionary (`tokens/variables/` + `tokens/styles/` → `build.js`).
- Never hardcode colors, spacing, typography, radius, shadows, border, blur, depth, or sizing.
- Never manually edit `src/theme/tokens.ts`.
- If a required token does not exist, report it before implementing — do not guess from Figma pixels.

## Figma MCP

- Use Figma MCP for structure, hierarchy, variants, and layout — not raw style values.
- Map Figma variables to tokens from `src/theme/tokens.ts`.
- Prefer variable-to-token mapping over visual approximation.

## Token Usage

```tsx
import { theme } from '../theme/tokens';
import { useTheme } from '../theme/useTheme';
import { getShadow } from '../theme/getShadow';

const t = useTheme();

// ✅ mode-aware colors
backgroundColor: t.color.background.neutral.surface
color: t.color.text.neutral.primary

// ✅ layout (Box props or theme.space / theme.radius)
<Box p="400" gap="200" radius="md" />

// ✅ typography — spread composite sets
<Text style={[t.typography['heading-m'], { color: t.color.text.neutral.primary }]} />

// ✅ shadows — use adapter
style={getShadow(t.elevation.sm)}

// ❌ never
backgroundColor: '#FF6600'
padding: 16
borderRadius: 8
```

Key namespaces: `color.*` (semantic + `palette`), `typography.*` (composites), `space`, `radius`, `border`, `elevation`. Space keys are `"100"`/`"400"`/`"n200"`, not `"md"`.

## Components

- `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` + `<Name>.stories.tsx` (CSF, both Storybooks).
- Use `<Box />` for layout; type-safe `keyof typeof theme.space` / `theme.radius`.
- Token-driven styling only; reuse existing components; web-compatible RN primitives only.
- Gate on `useAppFonts()` where fonts are needed.

## Missing Tokens

Stop → report missing token + suggested name/category → wait for confirmation before adding to `tokens/styles/typography.json`, `tokens/styles/elevation.json`, or requesting a Figma export.

## Workflow

1. Inspect in Figma (MCP) → 2. Map tokens → 3. Build component + props → 4. Add story → 5. Report gaps.

After any `tokens/` or `build.js` change, run `npm run build-tokens`.
